   "l": "One who knows does not speak,",
   "v": true,
   "n": "者 turns what precedes it into 'the one that ——s': 知者, 'the knower'. The couplet is a chiasmus — know, speak, speak, know — and that shape, rather than any argument, is what makes it stick.\n\nIt is not a rule of silence. Wang Bi's comment on this line is 因自然也, 'he goes by what is so of itself'; on the next it is 造事端也, 'he starts things up'. The one who knows has nothing to add to what is already the case.",
   "p": true
